{"abstract":"Past research on recognizing human affect has made use of a variety of physiological sensors in many ways. Nonetheless, how affective dynamics are influenced in the context of human daily life has not yet been explored. In this work, we present a wearable affective life-log system (ALIS), that is robust as well as easy to use in daily life to detect emotional changes and determine their cause-and-effect relationship on users' lives. The proposed system records how a user feels in certain situations during long-term activities with physiological sensors. Based on the long-term monitoring, the system analyzes how the contexts of the user's life affect his/her emotion changes. Furthermore, real-world experimental results demonstrate that the proposed wearable life-log system enables us to build causal structures to find effective stress relievers suited to every stressful situation in school life.","affiliations":[],"arxiv_id":"1911.01072","authors":["Byung Hyung Kim","Sungho Jo"],"availability":{"basis":"arxiv_public_full_text","checked_at":"2026-08-20T08:57:42+00:00","full_text_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1911.01072.pdf","license":"arxiv-distribution","page_count":13,"pdf_bytes":2897758,"status":"available"},"citation_count":null,"content_digest":"a4ccd6f35180816fcf0e3f30099cff61fd4fae6e3bc77d43eb3efe1e2143df7b","created_at":"2026-08-20T08:57:42+00:00","doi":"","identifier_observations":[],"institutions":[],"landing_url":"","legacy_ids":[],"migration_provenance":{"source_content_digest":"d5a7fde477b7b1d978d36b3372c7c455bcd2ea23f7c132f4593cc45d740825c6","source_schema_version":"global-work-v1"},"openalex_id":"","pmcid":"","pmid":"","publication_date":"","revision":1,"schema_version":"global-work-v2","semantic_scholar_id":"","source_urls":[],"status":"active","title":"Wearable Affective Life-Log System for Understanding Emotion Dynamics in Daily Life","updated_at":"2026-08-20T08:57:42+00:00","venue":"arXiv","work_id":"W-B90BB0077065","year":2019}
